  <static seed="377" source="Library/272/setStewart13_4/problem_1.pg">
    <statement><p>Given that the acceleration vector is 
<m>\mathbf{a} \left( t \right) = \left(
-9 \cos(3t), -9 \sin(3t),  -5t \right)</m>,</p>
<p>the initial velocity is <m>\mathbf{v}(0) = (1,0,1)</m>,</p>
<p>and the initial position vector is <m>\mathbf{r}(0) = (1,1,1)</m>, compute:</p>
<p>A. The velocity vector <m>\mathbf{v} \left( t \right) =</m> <fillin characters="15" name="AnSwEr0001"/> <m>\mathbf{i} +</m> <fillin characters="15" name="AnSwEr0002"/> <m>\mathbf{j} +</m> <fillin characters="15" name="AnSwEr0003"/> <m>\mathbf{k}</m></p>
<p>B. The position vector <m>\mathbf{r} \left( t \right) =</m> <fillin characters="15" name="AnSwEr0004"/> <m>\mathbf{i} +</m> <fillin characters="15" name="AnSwEr0005"/> <m>\mathbf{j} +</m> <fillin characters="15" name="AnSwEr0006"/> <m>\mathbf{k}</m></p>
<p>Note: Your answers must be functions of
<m>\mathbf{t}</m>; e.g.,  <lq/>5 cos(2t)<rq/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-3\sin\mathopen{}\left(3t\right)+1</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>3\cos\mathopen{}\left(3t\right)-3</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{-5t^{2}}{2}+1</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\cos\mathopen{}\left(3t\right)+t</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\sin\mathopen{}\left(3t\right)-3t+1</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{-5t^{3}}{6}+t+1</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
  </static>
